{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And they said.</b> Because they saw that they did as Aaron's deed with the serpent, and also with the plague of blood and the frog, and could not now do as Aaron did, they said to Pharaoh: This plague did not come for Israel's sake to send them, but it is a plague of Elohim according to the arrangement of the stars upon the astrological sign of the land of Egypt. For I have already explained that Pharaoh did not deny the Creator, only the Name that Moses mentioned to him. And this is like \"for His hand has not struck us; it was a chance that happened to us\" (1 Samuel 6:9) — from the heavens. Therefore Pharaoh's heart was strengthened. And that which strengthens this interpretation is that they said, \"It is the finger of Elohim,\" and did not say, \"the finger of YHWH,\" who is the God of Israel — as Pharaoh said in the plague of the frogs: \"Entreat YHWH\" (above, verse 4 [Exodus 8:4]). And this Name is mentioned in the latter plagues. Furthermore, Moses told Pharaoh the matter of the plague of the river before it happened, and likewise the plague of the frogs, but he did not mention to him the plague of the lice at the outset."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites Exodus 8:4 by its verse number within the chapter (פ' ד'), which corresponds to the phrase 'Entreat YHWH' in the plague of frogs."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:40.934708380Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}